{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Ukkhepakatavaccha","html":"<article id='thag1.65'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.65 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.65 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Sattamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Seven </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Ukkhepakatavacchattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Ukkhepakatavaccha </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ukkhepakatavacchassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Vaccha has tossed away </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṅkalitaṁ bahūhi vassehi; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>what he built over many years. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Taṁ bhāsati gahaṭṭhānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sitting comfortably, uplifted with joy, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sunisinno uḷārapāmojjo”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>he teaches this to householders. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Ukkhepakatavaccho thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
